#
# The session environment of a DESKTOP guest. leandro-display.service links
# this file to /run/environment.d/60-leandro-display.conf when it loads
# nvidia-drm, so it exists only while the virtual display does. gdm starts
# after that service, and both its greeter's gnome-shell and the autologin
# session's had the variable (measured 2026-09-16, Ubuntu 24.04, gdm 46).
#
# mutter on the legacy KMS API, not the atomic one. The virtual display is
# NVIDIA's DISPLAYLESS NVKMS path, and that path has no output LUT
# (nvkms-displayless.c, DisplaylessGetCapabilities sets no caps.olut), while
# nvidia-drm offers GAMMA_LUT on every CRTC regardless. A MODESET that carries
# a gamma LUT is accepted -- nvEvoSetLut records curOutputLutEnabled without
# asking the caps -- and from then on every flip inherits that LUT surface
# and fails ValidateHeadLutHwState (nvkms-hw-flip.c:1526). The compositor gets
# EINVAL for every frame, ~1000 a second, and the scanout never changes:
# the grey or black Sunshine stream. mutter 46 puts its colour-device gamma
# (a linear ramp) into the first modeset whenever colord answers before the
# first frame, as it did on this guest (measured 2026-09-16:
# "[atomic] Setting CRTC 59 property 'GAMMA_LUT' (28) to 67" in the
# ALLOW_MODESET commit, then "KMS update failed: drmModeAtomicCommit: Invalid
# argument" for every flip; with colord masked the same modeset sets the
# gamma "to bypass" and nothing fails). On the legacy API the gamma is its own
# drmModeCrtcSetGamma: it fails once, alone, and never reaches a modeset.
#
# Any other compositor that sets GAMMA_LUT in a modeset has the same problem;
# this line only covers mutter.
MUTTER_DEBUG_FORCE_KMS_MODE=simple
